#: ../../source/compliance.rst:2 116ce5846d934ae18ca788efa0f36644
msgid "_`Language compliance: what can be claimed today`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:4 0f7be70682aa453fa0a053993a57a4ff
msgid ""
"This page answers one question honestly: **which sentence about language "
"compliance may this project put in front of a customer today, and which "
"may it not put in front of anybody yet.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:8 09116ac55ecd4f86a867f091512bd35f
msgid ""
"It is deliberately short, and every claim on it points at a file or a "
"gate that can be re-run. A claim that cannot be re-run is not evidence, "
"it is a recollection -- and the whole point of the report is that the two"
" differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:15 06d84736f06b4d6482c867b146063898
msgid "The rule table"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:17 72d9535ed1864eacb225a8bb485bfb12
msgid ""
"``.github/project/compliance/rules.tsv`` is the claim, one rule per line."
" It is **generated**, from two inputs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:20 0d6b9c48a7294ce2b41b45402f134b6d
msgid ""
"``.github/project/compliance/tool-checks.txt`` -- a snapshot of the check"
" names the pinned ``.github/misc/.clang-tidy`` **names** in its "
"``Checks:`` block. The snapshot exists because a glob quietly matching "
"one more check adds a rule to the subset with nobody deciding to. It "
"records what that block names, not what the tool resolves it to -- see "
"the next section for why those are two different questions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:26 b9b65b284cc94e098a9bb787bd250d17
msgid ""
"``.github/project/compliance/rules-manual.json`` -- everything a tool "
"cannot decide: what the compiler flags enforce, what this repository's "
"own gates and tests enforce, which units have no behaviour to check, "
"which rules are deviated and which are open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:31 4dd78d4f1dbf402d9a88df08a336f459
msgid ""
"Regenerate with ``python3 .github/project/compliance/gen_subset.py``; "
"``--check`` reports drift instead of writing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:35 6a80d12fa42f40d580ab20241ac95cb2
msgid "The two lists, and why neither can answer alone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:37 3f7a9b51daf54678918fb7fd4c794596
msgid ""
"The pinned ``.github/misc/.clang-tidy`` is a **loose baseline of intent, "
"by design**. Its ``Checks:`` value is a folded scalar whose ``#`` lines "
"are literal, so ``clang-tidy --dump-config`` resolves the list to ``-*``:"
" the scaffold's own ``tidy`` gate compiles every source in ``src/`` and "
"constrains nothing. That is the template's posture rather than a defect, "
"and it is not a patch this project sends upstream: the private-domain "
"syntax of this repository (``// Conan::ImportStart`` and the rest) is "
"governed by the IaC layer -- the shared conventions, the codegen starter "
"and the skills -- so the linter is deliberately kept out of that argument"
" and stays compatible with whatever an instance decides."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:48 d2974da9d3f54e3685f637b672fa2d7b
msgid ""
"What follows from that is the part that matters to a reader of this page:"
" **the pinned file cannot be the answer to \"what is enforced\".** Two "
"facts are true at once, and the page would be misleading if it stated "
"either alone:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:52 89369e94bf9749e7942ee5052fc19359
msgid ""
"the pinned configuration **names** ``bugprone-*``, ``performance-*``, "
"``cert-*`` and two ``cppcoreguidelines-*`` checks, which is what ``tool-"
"checks.txt`` records;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:55 c29b88a055a14844b1617388c0c9f200
msgid ""
"the pinned configuration **runs** none of them, which is why ``enforce`` "
"exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:58 ecf0b0d4abb4447aaa607e2f332ea46b
msgid ""
"``.github/project/enforce.json`` is where this project declares its own "
"strictness. The gate composes a check set from **outside** the pinned "
"file -- ``clang-tidy --checks`` overrides the config's ``Checks`` key "
"while its ``CheckOptions`` and ``HeaderFilterRegex`` still apply -- so "
"the pinned file stays byte-identical and the families still run over "
"every target. The same file carries three things a reader needs: the "
"families that run, the checks exempted from a family (each with a signed "
"deviation permit, or the gate fails), and the checks this project has "
"looked at and decided **not** to run. That third list is a record with a "
"count and a reason per entry; an entry with no reason or no evidence "
"fails the gate, because an omission and a decision are otherwise "
"indistinguishable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:70 baa83755a11549d3ad76be13852bef02
msgid "Two consequences worth stating plainly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:72 f38b15bcf027419da15dd9a72ee2872d
msgid ""
"**``implemented`` in the rule table means \"a named mechanism runs it\", "
"and the mechanism for a lint rule is now the family table.** A check that"
" the pinned file names while nothing executes it is not an implemented "
"rule; it is a sentence about a file. The ``tidy:`` rows therefore "
"describe the pinned intent, and the rows whose enforcement comes from "
"``enforce`` say so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:77 004ee86b1f564b20af15045497807a36
msgid ""
"**\"This check is on\" is a claim about a run, not about a "
"configuration.** The witness is ``python3 .github/project/gates.py "
"enforce``, which fails if any target does not compile, reports any "
"diagnostic from the extra families, and runs a positive control: a "
"scratch file that must be diagnosed with the families on and must be "
"clean with them off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:84 8f6ae95ea17b48f0b63c850ea814523e
msgid "The four counts, and what each one means"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:86 347957fc2b4d416e962053734ec5285a
msgid ""
"The ``subset`` gate (``python3 .github/project/gates.py subset``) prints "
"the same four numbers and refuses to pass unless they add up to the "
"number of rows, so a rule that matched no status surfaces as an "
"arithmetic failure rather than as a line nobody notices is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:95 ded2bc8f917b423ea7b1d6312b625676
msgid "Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:96 bf3d849aac304e1fa540272b8553f1f5
msgid "Means"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:97 f2c8eb9c52b945c69e961f8415ce3a73
msgid "What makes it legal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:98 9e88e9fba41546e0bc136a625c494e9e
msgid "``implemented``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:99 b36eee1eb0274971bf6a55a89c3bba51
msgid "something enforces it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:100 2f8605b0223e477cbff5e86d79ec70b7
msgid ""
"the ``check`` column names the mechanism, in one of four forms: "
"``tidy:<check>`` (a check the pinned config enables), ``gate:<name>`` (a "
"gate that exists), ``test:<file>`` (a test file that exists) or "
"``case:<id>`` (a case in the negative-compilation set). A row whose "
"``check`` names nothing that exists fails the build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:105 fe284434b50042fdb9224649f8b37caf
msgid "``not-applicable``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:106 bb5eaea14cbc4b5aa4dc255c2a116756
msgid "there is nothing to enforce"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:107 a1f9eef5e7274fdaa5f4a52f734269b4
msgid ""
"two sub-cases, told apart by the ``delta`` column. ``delta: none`` means "
"the unit has no behaviour: an interface, a lookup table or a test double "
"-- the thirteen terminal ``L1`` modules of the claim table in the project"
" ``README.md``. ``delta: vacuous`` means the language feature is rejected"
" by the build (exceptions, RTTI), so a rule about it has no operand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:113 26cc4b04d27744d9b1cc8a80541c7530
msgid "``deviation``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:114 6a988a3beecd4eb8a524eb192ffac85f
msgid "we do not follow it, on purpose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:115 b304759c82f145f4b29bebf7617b4a78
msgid ""
"``.github/project/compliance/deviation/<rule>.md`` exists and carries all"
" five elements: reason, impact, compensating control, approver, review "
"date. Missing one element fails the build, and so does a ``NOLINT`` in "
"the shipped tree with no record -- and a record with no suppression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:119 1c6ff4b4496548a1b3da46464eadeb1c
msgid "``open``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:120 4e7d1733d336455c932a9bb42f4dec8f
msgid "we intend to have it and do not"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:121 97cb6d354fc04a67ad0d53e929bbf839
msgid ""
"this count may only fall. ``.github/project/compliance/subset-"
"baseline.json`` freezes it; raising it means re-freezing the baseline in "
"the same commit, which is a review event rather than an accident."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:125 07d99943aeb840feb100b31ef0f85f71
msgid ""
"``.github/project/compliance/COMPLIANCE-SUMMARY.md`` renders the same "
"four counts for a delivery package, plus the per-source breakdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:129 ac8679c31e6149ba93b0901e338b55fc
msgid "What can be said today"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:138 fe1cebd7fb0740e090a23b0077f1ef41
msgid ""
"The numbers are not written here on purpose: they are the output of the "
"gate and of ``COMPLIANCE-SUMMARY.md``, and a number copied into prose is "
"a second source of truth with a shelf life. Read them from the gate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:142 ebe81a82de6d451686ab73665d6f4518
msgid ""
"Two sentences that follow directly, because each has a re-runnable "
"witness:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:144 a6b7cbd088e94992a0bcfd1e2257cc3e
msgid ""
"**Ignoring a C ABI error code is a build failure.** The witness is a real"
" compilation, not a syntax check: ``python3 "
".github/project/negative_compile.py`` runs ``c_abi_dropped_error_code`` "
"with ``-Werror`` and requires the diagnostic. It also pins the counter-"
"intuitive part: a ``(void)`` cast does **not** silence "
"``warn_unused_result`` on GCC, while binding the value first does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:150 d5d69e0c0feb4139ad19835be24c7bdf
msgid ""
"**The rule set cannot drift from the pinned tool configuration.** The "
"witness is ``python3 .github/project/gates.py subset``, which compares "
"the enabled check set against ``tool-checks.txt`` and refuses a row that "
"names a check the block does not name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:154 2167f4a9456d4348bb2c5b8fe94856f3
msgid ""
"**The CERT C++ family runs, and the pinned file did not need to change.**"
" The witness is ``python3 .github/project/gates.py enforce``, which "
"composes the check set from that block and from the family table and "
"requires every target to compile and to produce no diagnostic from the "
"extra families. The family was measured at zero on the source before it "
"was switched on; the three sites it found on the way were fixed rather "
"than suppressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:162 4ddf3834ef8a471aa7685cfd731af4ca
msgid "What cannot be said yet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:168 64803d6923b44ecaa2ca797b750444fa
msgid "Sentence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:169 ad5af60b0bab4c2aace3b02c8a38176c
msgid "Why not, and what would close it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:170 698e5897f7d643fe80127c2165128637
msgid ""
"\"Organised per MISRA C++:2023: N implemented / M not applicable / K "
"deviated\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:172 7d9d1cfec8c84f39931345374fc08bf4
msgid ""
"The four categories are exactly the ones MISRA Compliance:2020 asks for, "
"and the deviation permits already carry its five elements -- but the "
"mapping from tool check to MISRA rule number does not exist, so N/M/K "
"cannot be filled in. That is the ``misra-rule-mapping`` row of the "
"``open`` register, and it is the difference between T0 and T1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:177 c68891664e8e4db28a03bebfd64b6005
msgid "\"Compliant with MISRA C++:2023\", or any ASIL / SIL / Class B level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:178 486e419775ef4c7ba1bd8ce8311bd0d5
msgid ""
"Levels are derived from the whole machine's hazard analysis and safety "
"goals. A library has no such context, so it can supply evidence about its"
" own behaviour and nothing about the level of the system it lands in. See"
" :ref:`honest limits <honest-limits>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:182 a68fbdbee14c4172861b03c63bd80153
msgid "\"Independently verified\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:183 4315934de43d471fb7e027d418f62b0a
msgid ""
"One author plus tooling can produce reproducibility, which is what this "
"repository does produce: a third party who clones it and runs the gates "
"gets the same numbers. It cannot produce independence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:186 682a9d8e05694313ad41536e97df77bc
msgid "\"Every check in the pinned configuration is enforced\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/compliance.rst:187 09e0202cd4f84d9cb25980f2fdc11291
msgid ""
"The configuration states an intent and the resolver discards it, so the "
"two are separate questions and only the second one is evidence. What this"
" repo enforces is in the family table, and the family table is not the "
"whole of that block: the checks it names but no gate executes are "
"recorded as ``open`` in the rule table, not as ``implemented``."
msgstr ""

